@page "/dropdown-filtering"

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H2" TagName="TagName.H1" class="rz-pt-8">
    Blazor DropDown filtering case sensitivity and filter operator
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    Add search to the Blazor DropDown with built-in filtering - choose the filter operator (contains, starts with), toggle case sensitivity, or filter data on demand.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenExample ComponentName="DropDown" Example="DropDownFiltering">
    <DropDownFiltering />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="dropdown-filtering#loaddata-event" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-8">
    Custom filtering with <strong>LoadData</strong> event
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-4">
    Use the <code>LoadData</code> event to implement custom filtering logic and load data on-demand.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenAlert AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Info" Variant="Variant.Flat" Shade="Shade.Lighter" AllowClose="false" class="rz-mb-8">
    With <code>LoadData</code> the <code>Data</code> collection holds only the current search results. When <code>ValueProperty</code> is set, the DropDown finds the selected item by looking up <code>Value</code> in <code>Data</code>, so the selected text disappears while the search results do not include that item and returns when they do. This example binds <code>Value</code> to the item itself (no <code>ValueProperty</code>) to keep the selected text visible while filtering. To keep using <code>ValueProperty</code>, include the selected item in the data returned by <code>LoadData</code>.
</RadzenAlert>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="DropDown" Example="DropDownFilteringLoadData">
    <DropDownFilteringLoadData />
</RadzenExample>